1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
I wanted to kill him, because my heart was broken.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:08,000
There was nothing between us.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:11,500
So afterward, I could not call it love.

4
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:14,000
But you do not need permission to have your heart broken.

5
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Heartbreak was the only thing I knew for certain I had ever had.

6
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:24,500
I cannot remember when I began doing things for two, alone.

7
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:31,000
Buying just enough groceries for free delivery. Cooking just enough to leave half behind.

8
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:36,500
When I tipped that half into the bin, I would hesitate for an instant.

9
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:42,500
As if tomorrow he might still drop by for dinner, the way he used to.

10
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:46,000
I chewed over that kindness for a long time.

11
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:49,000
He was like that with everyone. I knew.

12
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:52,000
But I refused to swallow it.

13
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,000
That day, his parents came to pick him up.

14
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:00,500
The three of them stood together, talking about something, laughing with ease.

15
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:05,000
I dragged my suitcase toward the coach, alone.

16
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:07,000
Very slowly.

17
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:09,500
I was waiting for him to call me back.

18
00:01:09,500 --> 00:01:13,500
To run over and introduce me to his parents.

19
00:01:13,500 --> 00:01:16,500
Of course I knew it would not happen.

20
00:01:16,500 --> 00:01:24,500
But the body has a mind of its own. It insisted on walking that slowly.

21
00:01:24,500 --> 00:01:33,500
By the time I had boarded the coach, taken a window seat and looked outside, they were long gone.

22
00:01:33,500 --> 00:01:38,000
Toward the end, I sent him a lot of messages.

23
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:43,500
He did not reply to a single one.

24
00:01:43,500 --> 00:01:47,500
Later, I typed what I wanted to say into my notes.

25
00:01:47,500 --> 00:01:52,500
Long entries and short ones, several thousand words in all.

26
00:01:52,500 --> 00:01:57,000
My phone buzzed in my pocket, and I wanted to take it out right away.

27
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:01,500
I still waited until I had left the shop before taking out my phone.

28
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:09,500
Nothing.

29
00:02:09,500 --> 00:02:12,500
The dream came later.

30
00:02:12,500 --> 00:02:16,000
At the graduation ball, the crowd had drifted away and the lights had come on.

31
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:21,000
He walked toward me in a black suit, a smile in his eyes.

32
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:24,500
We sat together, teasing each other.

33
00:02:24,500 --> 00:02:29,000
Then his hand touched my neck, and he kissed me softly.

34
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:36,000
That kiss became the only goodbye we ever had.

35
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:42,500
After that, I saw people who looked like him from behind, in supermarkets, on the metro, at the cinema.

36
00:02:42,500 --> 00:02:47,500
Once, someone turned sideways to let another person pass.

37
00:02:47,500 --> 00:02:51,500
I saw his face and knew I had mistaken him for someone else.

38
00:02:51,500 --> 00:02:56,500
But I still waited for him to turn away and looked at his back once more.

39
00:02:56,500 --> 00:02:59,500
Soon, a second him appeared.

40
00:02:59,500 --> 00:03:03,500
Back then, we had not yet started eating together every week.
